+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Apply the v7.0.124 update to a v7.0.123 installation.
+
+Two reports after v7.0.123, plus nine defects found by auditing the shipped suite against a real FFmpeg:
+
+1. "its not generating video with 3 language" - the editions WERE being made; they were never allowed to count
+   as finished. ``_captions_contradict()`` compared the burned-caption evidence with the job's wish in both
+   directions, but only one of them is evidence: a caption is not on screen every second, so sampled frames
+   that find no text prove nothing (``engine/render/caption_check.explain()`` has always said so, and the
+   render loop only ever sets ``captions_disputed`` for the visible-text direction). A language whose
+   transcript was ON was therefore pending again on every single run whenever a bright picture hid its
+   glyphs from the heuristic: a new export folder each time, the previous file stamped "not the current
+   video", and the Three-language panel reporting ``exported`` while the renderer reported ``pending``. The
+   contradiction is now one-directional, and an ``exported`` entry with no readable path can no longer raise
+   ``ValueError`` out of the whole edition loop.
+
+2. "can we do something which will not show me the annoying pop-up chromium browser during the video
+   generation process ... i have to stop the video generation" while sharing a screen - Quiet browser worked
+   on Linux/WSL and raised ``Quiet browser currently supports Linux/WSL only`` everywhere else, so on Windows
+   the popup was unavoidable. ``engine/quiet_browser.py`` now hides a browser on every OS and stays headed
+   everywhere: Windows/macOS park a real window at ``--window-position=-32000,-32000`` with ``--mute-audio``
+   (never ``--headless`` - Google refuses a headless sign-in), and *Show browser* moves that same running
+   window on screen over a loopback debugging port instead of restarting anything. A sign-in wall reveals the
+   hidden window by itself and hides it again once signed in, so a session is never hidden while it needs you.
+
+3. The Uploads picker lost the contract its own tests were written for: with no identifiable picker it fell
+   back to clicking *Uploads* in Flow's MAIN SIDEBAR - navigating away from the project mid-generation - and
+   its ``timeout_ms`` parameter was gone. It is bounded by one deadline again, strictly scoped, and retries an
+   unstable tab through its clickable ancestor without ``force``.
+
+4. ``render_overlay_png()`` drew the playful channel-name pill AND composited the logo, where
+   ``build_overlay_assets()`` also schedules a separate logo overlay - three channel marks per frame. A
+   channel logo IS the channel mark: with one available the badge is not drawn at all.
+
+5. Project deletion did a blocking ``wait_for(state='visible')`` on the first menu item (*Rename*), so a menu
+   that was merely slow to animate raised "No explicit success confirmation" before *Delete* was ever clicked;
+   Gemini review handed the file chooser a one-element list where a bare path was expected; three
+   ``st.dataframe`` calls used the deprecated ``use_container_width``; and the Create step-4 selectbox had been
+   renamed away from ``TTS``, which is what the Music-only dashboard test looks for.
+
+Usage (run from the existing installation folder, after extracting the 7.0.124 zip beside it):
+
+    python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.124-Finished-Editions-And-Quiet-Browser/tools/update_v7123_to_v7124.py .         # dry run
+    python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.124-Finished-Editions-And-Quiet-Browser/tools/update_v7123_to_v7124.py . --apply # install
+
+Only code, documentation and tests are replaced. Outputs, saved jobs, speech batches, language editions and
+their exports, Flow journals and request files, character photos, channel profiles, browser profiles and
+``music_library/`` are never copied, moved or deleted. Stop the dashboard before --apply.
+"""
+
+import argparse
+import datetime
+import fcntl
+import hashlib
+import json
+import os
+import shutil
+import tempfile
+from pathlib import Path
+
+CHANGES = [
+    'VERSION',
+    'app.py',
+
+    'engine/quiet_browser.py',
+    'engine/providers/flow_browser.py',
+    'engine/flow_music.py',
+
+    'engine/language_editions.py',
+    'engine/render/graphics.py',
+    'engine/channel_desk_ui.py',
+
+    'engine/flow_project_delete.py',
+    'engine/providers/gemini_web.py',
+
+    'tests/test_v7124_quiet_browser_all_os.py',
+    'tests/test_v7124_three_language_convergence.py',
+
+    'FINISHED_EDITIONS_AND_QUIET_BROWSER_V7_0_124.md',
+    'REFERENCE_VIDEO_RESEARCH_2026_11_02.md',
+    'tools/update_v7123_to_v7124.py',
+]
+
+# Files as they exist in 7.0.123: the only hashes this updater will replace.
+# A hash outside this list means local edits; the file is preserved and nothing is applied.
+ALLOWED = {
+    'VERSION': [
+        'b9f9cf3ba03112809ae93aff7d14eee61e1858ea7696034debe0004f60d2fe8d'],
+    'app.py': [
+        'f1e6296cea30162c24291e8d37347fe93effcadf128c99c43423fed9dae1dd19'],
+    'engine/channel_desk_ui.py': [
+        'e225ca5c5c30f23c151526a1bc9716e47e1f8a60216c27a85d215cec6a5d5f5a'],
+    'engine/flow_music.py': [
+        '91f9fc255c25c8714f16a28f44f8a2e39e37498d8d079b538dca3d0a40ccca65'],
+    'engine/flow_project_delete.py': [
+        '586baee4e4c2d1ffa0c5ca91d85a53b072c25274c46caaee72c24d2de8b7442c'],
+    'engine/language_editions.py': [
+        'd1f715b6c17076d0e5bdf42e1b06c10c1f5025b897476802091a80bf47fba063'],
